`acceptor` is a pure decision core: stdlib-only, deterministic, with no I/O
beyond the JSONL ledger it is handed a path to.  `pytest` (the [test] extra) is
the only development dependency.

The statistical machinery implements and extends published methods, which are
cited in the module docstrings and in README.md:

  * paired testing by betting / anytime-valid e-processes
      PACE (arXiv 2606.08106); Waudby-Smith & Ramdas (2024);
      Howard, Ramdas, McAuliffe & Sekhon (2021); Ville's inequality
  * the summable error-budget (CTHS) schedule, Z = 3.387735532
      SEA (arXiv 2607.00871)
  * "mechanical rejection overrides LLM approval, never the reverse"
      the PROCTOR rule

Those works belong to their authors; this is an independent implementation.
